# Conditional Access Baseline

## Purpose

Document the initial Microsoft Entra Conditional Access baseline for Kile Business Systems.

## Initial policy set

| Policy | Purpose | Initial state |
|---|---|---|
| CA001 | Require MFA for users | Report-only |
| CA002 | Block legacy authentication | Report-only |
| CA003 | Protect privileged administrators | Report-only |

## Deployment method

1. Design the policy.
2. Configure exclusions for the emergency-access account where appropriate.
3. Set the policy to Report-only.
4. Generate representative sign-ins.
5. Review Entra sign-in logs and Conditional Access results.
6. Correct unintended impact.
7. Enable one policy at a time.
8. Monitor after enforcement.
9. Document the final state.

## General standards

- Prefer All resources for broad baseline protection unless a specific exception is justified.
- Avoid stacking multiple unvalidated changes.
- Keep a tested emergency-access path.
- Use least privilege for administrator targeting.
- Record material changes in `CHANGELOG.md`.
